  "summary": "All 8 results inbox items worked and closed per RBC-INBOX-01. Each patient was confirmed by name plus DOB or MRN.\n1. Raj Patel (pt-0006), positive FIT: Dr. Lin's GI colonoscopy referral sr-t2-gi-1020 is still active, so I linked it and did not place another (RBC-GI-01 §2). Patient messaged, note written.\n2. Leslie Parisian (pt-0007), renal US: simple 1.8 cm cyst and the report says no follow-up. Closed with a comment that no follow-up is needed (RBC-INBOX-01 §3).\n3–4. Edra Ondricka (pt-0016), TSH and lipid panel: all values normal. Acknowledged and closed.\n5. Linda Marsh (pt-0013), St. Brigid ED CT A/P from 2026-06-04: incidental 5 mm RLL nodule. It is already followed in lung cancer screening (Lung-RADS 2 on LDCT 2025-09-15), so the incidental-nodule table doesn't apply. Her next LDCT window (due 2026-09-15 ±1 month) has passed, so I ordered the LDCT within 14 days (sr-t0007, 10/23–11/06). Tracking task task-t0008 is due 11/06, the patient was messaged, and a note was written (RBC-RAD-05 §2 and §4).\n6. Tomás Ruiz (pt-0053, minor), knee X-ray: aggressive lytic lesion of the distal femur, suspected bone tumour. Under RBC-RAD-05 §3 I ordered an urgent MRI of the femur with and without contrast (sr-t0012) and an urgent orthopaedic oncology referral (sr-t0013), both for 10/23–11/05. Tracking tasks task-t0014 and task-t0015 are due 11/05. I created an urgent task for J. Reyes NP (task-t0016) to call his mother today. I also sent an urgent message to the family with activity limits and when to seek urgent care, and wrote a note.\n7. Walter Brennan (pt-0008), K 6.4 on a hemolyzed sample: urgent repeat BMP ordered for no later than Mon 10/26 (sr-t0020). Patient messaged to come in, on-call not notified, note written (RBC-LAB-03 §2).\n8. Denise Holloway (pt-0010), K 6.2, not hemolyzed: pool-oncall messaged at stat priority and a STAT BMP ordered (sr-t0021), per RBC-LAB-03 §1. Her creatinine rose to 1.58 from 1.46, and lisinopril was started 10/06. I didn't